---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="The story behind Belongary and why it exists.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-plum mb-8">About Belongary</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-lg">
        Belongary was born from a simple observation: the people who most need to know whether they'll belong at a company are the least likely to get an honest answer before they accept the offer.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-cream rounded-xl border border-border p-8 my-8">
        <p class="text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-plum mb-3">
          "Would you tell someone like you to take this job?"
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/60">
          That's the question we ask. Not "rate your employer." Not "how many stars." Just: would you recommend this place to someone who shares your identity, your background, your lens on the world?
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Employer branding is polished. Glassdoor reviews are generic. Neither tells a Black woman whether she'll be sponsored for leadership, or tells a neurodivergent engineer whether the culture actually accommodates different working styles, or tells a working parent whether flexibility is real or performative.
      </p>

      <p>
        Belongary exists because belonging isn't one thing. It's different for everyone, and the only people qualified to report on it are the people living it. We built a platform that respects that complexity:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-ink/70">
        <li>Identity lenses you choose, not demographic boxes we impose</li>
        <li>No work-email verification — we don't gatekeep who gets to speak</li>
        <li>Suppression thresholds that protect anonymity while showing honest numbers</li>
        <li>Your words, unedited — we reject, we never rewrite</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-semibold text-plum mt-10 mb-4">The Vision</h2>

      <p>
        We started with healthcare because it's an industry where belonging gaps have real consequences — for workers and for patients. But Belongary is for every industry, every company, every worker who's ever wondered whether they'd truly fit.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our goal isn't to shame companies. It's to create a feedback loop that makes workplaces better. When companies see how belonging scores differ across identity lenses, they have actionable data to close those gaps. When workers can see those scores before accepting an offer, they can make informed decisions.
      </p>

      <p>
        Truth, filtered through the lenses that matter. That's Belongary.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a href="/review" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3 bg-coral text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-coral/90 transition-colors shadow-sm">
          Add Your Voice
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
